{
  "schema": "starcrew.system/1",
  "_doc": "A star system (openspec/changes/patrol-mission design 2; flight-and-navigation 13's system file): the system frame has its origin at the star's centre, x and z in the plane of the planets, +y north; positions are metres. The bodies stand where they are at the mission's epoch (rails, flight-and-navigation 8, come later). A station is one of the spacedock versions (openspec/changes/spacedock design 11a: `version` A-E, `data/space/spacedock.json` its sizes), set at orbit_radius_m from its body's centre along orbit_dir, or at offset_m from a point (near); its attitude turns its own frame into the system's (the spacedock frame: origin at its centre, +z the way its doors face, E's +z on the star); its mass lock is measured from its frame's origin; its arrival point is in its own frame; a berth is a pose in the station's frame (where the docked Tern's origin sits, and its attitude there) and a departure path in the berth's own frame (the docked Tern's), each leg ending at a point with the most it may be flown at, so a berth works whatever shape its station has. A point of interest's arrival point is an offset from it, where a jump to it ends. A body's look is the sky program's planet (data/space/exterior.json's fields). Read by sc-core::system.",
